Summary (Uddana) of that [chapter]:

Kama and Guha, and Duttha, and Suddha, and Parama Jara;
Metteyya and Pasura, and Magandiya, and Purabheda;
Kalaha, and the two Byuha, and again Tuvattaka;
Attadanda as the foremost sutta, questioned by the Elder — sixteen [suttas].
Thus these suttas [form] the entire Atthakavagga.
